From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camel: keep the S/MIME header out of the gir scan when disabled

camel-smime-context.c compiles to nothing when S/MIME is off, since its whole
body is inside #ifdef ENABLE_SMIME, but camel-smime-context.h declares the
type either way. g-ir-scanner reads the header, emits a reference to the type
function, and the temporary binary it links has nothing to resolve it against:

  undefined reference to `camel_smime_context_get_type'

Drop the pair from the scanner's source list when S/MIME is disabled. The
files stay in the build - the header still installs, and the one function that
lives outside the guard is still compiled.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/src/camel/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/camel/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -355,6 +355,18 @@
 add_pkgconfig_file(camel.pc.in camel-${API_VERSION}.pc)
 
 set(gir_sources ${SOURCES} ${HEADERS})
+
+# Without S/MIME, camel-smime-context.c compiles to nothing - its whole body
+# sits inside #ifdef ENABLE_SMIME - while camel-smime-context.h still declares
+# the type unconditionally. The scanner reads the header, emits a reference to
+# camel_smime_context_get_type(), and the temporary binary it links fails:
+#
+#   undefined reference to `camel_smime_context_get_type'
+#
+# Keep the pair out of the scan when there is nothing behind it.
+if(NOT ENABLE_SMIME)
+	list(REMOVE_ITEM gir_sources camel-smime-context.c camel-smime-context.h)
+endif(NOT ENABLE_SMIME)
 set(gir_identifies_prefixes Camel camel)
 set(gir_includes GObject-2.0 Gio-2.0 libxml2-2.0)
 set(gir_cflags -DCAMEL_COMPILATION)
